{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Only, etc.</b> These are the words of the prophet, as though saying: I did not know these future things by way of wisdom, but by YHWH alone who said to me these righteous deeds and the might. The correct reading is: 'Only in YHWH alone are righteousness and might,' and the word לי entered by scribal error, and the meaning is 'by the name [of the one] who spoke with me.'" "<b>His witnesses.</b> [Like] 'and you did not return to Me' (Amos 4:6)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ונכנסה מלת לי אמר' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. It appears to address a superfluous לי in the received text, possibly referencing a variant reading.", 1 "Ibn Ezra glosses עדיו as equivalent to עדי in Amos 4:6, where the same root is read as 'to Me' (lit. 'My witness/testimony'), understood as divine object suffix."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:16.936805206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}